		<label>Type 80 GPMG</label>
		<description>Caliber: 7.62x54mmR. 100-round bullet link. Select-Fire.

The Type 80 is a Chinese copy of the Soviet PK machine gun. The PK was not originally adopted in China due to the Sino-Soviet split of the 1960s, forcing the PLA to instead turn to the indigenous Type 67 design. However, China came upon examples of the machine guns from some source during the 1970s, and made the decision to reverse engineer them to produce the Type 80 GPMG, which supplemented the Type 67 in service. The Type 80 is outwardly quite similar to the Soviet PKM, using the older flash hider and featuring polymer furniture. Now designated "QJY-80" in Chinese service, the weapon has been widely exported, and a variant in 7.62x51mm NATO known as the CS/LM4 even exists for the same purpose.</description>
